# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
# Dustfile — Cleanup and hygiene contract for progblocks
# Author: Jonathan D.A. Jewell (hyperpolymath)
#
# What should be cleaned up (exnovated) or clearly re-labelled. Housekeeping,
# not blockers — see ../bust/Bustfile.a2ml for what's actually broken.

@abstract:
Cleanup and hygiene items for progblocks. Two dead-code items dominate:
view-manager.js (never imported by anything) and the tree-sitter-a2ml.wasm
placeholder (not real WebAssembly). Neither is a runtime bug on its own —
both are exnovation candidates that currently mislead a reader of the
source tree into thinking more is wired up than actually is.
@end

## Dead Code

### view-manager-unreferenced
- description: src/modules/view-manager.js (55 lines) is never imported by anything in this tree, yet contains the only real linter/WebSocket code — the rendered linter panel in prog-block.js is instead a hardcoded '<i>Linter ready</i>' string
- run: "! grep -rl 'view-manager' src/prog-block.js src/modules/exporter.js src/modules/smart-paste.js src/a2ml-parser.js src/k9-validator.js 2>/dev/null | grep -q ."
- severity: warning
- enforced-by: not yet automated (documentary)
- notes: Two honest paths forward — wire it in and make the linter real, or delete it and stop implying live-linting exists. Doing neither is the current state.

### a2ml-parser-stub
- description: src/a2ml-parser.js (60 lines) has its tree-sitter path commented out; the A2MLState class is dead code; the parse function is never called by the component
- run: grep -q 'tree-sitter' src/a2ml-parser.js
- severity: warning
- enforced-by: not yet automated (documentary)

### wasm-placeholder
- description: assets/tree-sitter-a2ml.wasm is a 118-byte ASCII text placeholder ("// Dummy WASM file placeholder"), not real WebAssembly
- run: test "$(stat -c%s assets/tree-sitter-a2ml.wasm 2>/dev/null || stat -f%z assets/tree-sitter-a2ml.wasm)" -lt 1000
- severity: warning
- enforced-by: not yet automated (documentary)
- notes: Either vendor a real compiled artefact or remove the file — a fake .wasm sitting in assets/ implies a working parser that does not exist.

### fake-validator-methods
- description: k9-validator.js's validateNickel() fakes a 50ms setTimeout then unconditionally returns {valid:true, errors:[]}; executeJustTask() console.logs and returns true. Neither is called by anything.
- run: grep -q 'setTimeout' src/k9-validator.js
- severity: warning
- enforced-by: not yet automated (documentary)

## Version Drift

### version-string-disagreement
- description: package.k9 and contracts.ncl say 1.0.0; progblocks.launcher.a2ml and progblocks-launcher.sh say 0.1.0; package.json says 0.3.0 — nothing has actually been released under any of these
- run: grep -q '"1.0.0"' contracts.ncl && grep -q '0.1.0' progblocks.launcher.a2ml
- severity: warning
- enforced-by: not yet automated (documentary)
- notes: Resolve to one version before any tag is cut — see ../descriptiles/PLAYBOOK.a2ml release-process.

## Build Recipe Honesty

### fake-build-recipe (RESOLVED — recipe removed)
- description: Justfile's build recipe used to cat-concatenate ES modules into one file without stripping import/export syntax, producing a file that could not run as a script. Rather than fix it, the recipe was deleted; there is no `build:` recipe in the Justfile at all now.
- run: "! grep -q '^build:' Justfile"
- severity: info
- enforced-by: this probe
- notes: If a real bundle step is ever needed, use a real bundler (esbuild) — do not re-add a recipe that only implies one exists.
